body:
DEC06 DONE (2124/2124). Interface items for the lead, no action needed to keep my package green (I declare them in my own header per n2_apple.h own rule and list them in vt/dec/symbols.txt), but they should land before the decoder dylib is wired into a payload:

  extern CMTime CMSampleBufferGetPresentationTimeStamp(CMSampleBufferRef sb);            /* pts -> token pairing */
  extern const CFStringRef kCMFormatDescriptionExtension_SampleDescriptionExtensionAtoms; /* avcC/hvcC atoms */
  extern CFTypeRef CMFormatDescriptionGetExtension(CMFormatDescriptionRef fmt, CFStringRef key);
  extern OSStatus CMVideoFormatDescriptionGetHEVCParameterSetAtIndex(CMFormatDescriptionRef fmt, size_t index,
      const uint8_t **ps, size_t *size, size_t *count, int *nalLength);
  extern CFTypeID CFDataGetTypeID(void);
  extern const uint8_t *CFDataGetBytePtr(CFDataRef data);
  extern CFIndex CFDataGetLength(CFDataRef data);

All seven are real iOS 16 exports (the ios import audit covers six of them; CFDataGetLength/BytePtr/TypeID were mapped in the audit through the supplementary TBD). P04 symbols.txt already proposes the HEVC accessor; the other six are new. Suggested text is exactly the block above.

Second item: include/n2vcd_proto.h is still rev 1, so DEC05 client/dec/n2vcd_dec.c cannot compile in the tree (it #errors on purpose) and my product adapter (vt/dec/n2vtd_client_dec05.c) is an empty TU until rev 2. DEC05 posted the paste-ready text: daemon/dec/n2vcd_proto_dec_rev2.h.txt (32-byte DEC_ADD_BUFFER with c_handle/c_bytes, OPEN.flags bits 8..15 layout, PICTURE_OK last word = poc, N2VCD_PROTO_REV2 2u). My run_tests.sh stages it in /tmp and proves DEC05 client + my adapter compile and link against it. Landing it makes the real client the default automatically; nothing else in my package changes.

Also for the build: SLIMRegister is visibility(default) and the linked dylib exports it; the six objects to compile are in vt/dec/STATUS.md §Integration. The plug-in is a separate file /System/Library/VideoDecoders/Slim.videodecoder per the opus-dec3 two-dylib proposal, gated by /private/var/db/nord2-video-hwdec. Fallback is CreateInstance -12913 (VT then tries H264SW/VCPHEVC); StartSession errors are fatal to the VTDecompressionSession (DEC08 [V]), so the 250 ms daemon probe lives in CreateInstance only.

No phone, nothing published.
